From b654b2d167ae28c3cba4f7c5e0e145a3970419b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?J=C3=B6rg=20Thalheim?= <joerg@thalheim.io>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:35:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] terminal.select: add a block mode for rectangular selections
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A keyboard copy mode can select cells, words and lines but not a
column range, which tmux and the herdr TUI offer as rectangle
selection. Ghostty's selection already carries a rectangle flag, so
expose it as mode "block".

The mode takes the opposite corner as `end` instead of relying on
terminal.adjust_selection: the native left/right/down adjustments skip
empty cells, so a rectangle could not reach padding or blank rows.

Signed-off-by: Jörg Thalheim <joerg@thalheim.io>
---
 src/commands.rs |  2 +-
 src/terminal.rs | 10 ++++++++--
 src/vt.rs       | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

